CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#154","metadata":{"content":"el Flujo CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#155","metadata":{"content":"l Flujo CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#156","metadata":{"content":"Flujo CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#157","metadata":{"content":"Flujo CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#158","metadata":{"content":"lujo CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#159","metadata":{"content":"ujo CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#16","metadata":{"content":"ected-hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#160","metadata":{"content":"jo CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#161","metadata":{"content":"o CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#162","metadata":{"content":"CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#163","metadata":{"content":"CCDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#164","metadata":{"content":"CDD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#165","metadata":{"content":"DD","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#166","metadata":{"content":"D","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#167","metadata":{"content":"1. **Garantiza la persistencia de políticas bajo presión de tokens**: Al fijar los slots de entorno y sistema con prioridad máxima (`0` y `1`) y el mensaje del usuario con prioridad `4`, el sistema asegura que bajo estrés de tokens la entrada del usuario se trunca *antes* que las directivas de seguridad. Esto mitiga la *omisión* de políticas por desbordamiento de contexto, pero **no** sustituye la robustez del modelo frente a inyección semántica que sí cabe en el presupuesto (ver `ccdd_spec_v0.3.md` §6, Consideraciones de Seguridad).\n2. **Independencia Tecnológica**: El contrato de contexto es puramente declarativo. El equipo de ingeniería puede migrar de LangChain a LangGraph, o de Python a Go, sin reescribir las políticas o la estructura de los prompts.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#168","metadata":{"content":"ir las políticas o la estructura de los prompts. *(Demostrado: `ccdd export --format openai|anthropic|text` emite el mismo contrato en el formato nativo de cada framework — la implementación de referencia lo prueba, no solo lo afirma.)*\n3. **QA y Auditoría Determinista**: Convierte el problema difuso de \"evaluar prompts\" en un conjunto de métricas verificables bit-a-bit en CI.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#17","metadata":{"content":"cted-hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#18","metadata":{"content":"ted-hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#19","metadata":{"content":"ed-hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#2","metadata":{"content":"ntiene el ojo, y la IA *informa pero no decide*.\n\nEl resultado: la IA entrega trabajo **acompañado de su verificación**, con la frontera entre *\"esto está comprobado\"* y *\"esto es criterio\"* dibujada de forma honesta. El humano sabe exactamente **hasta dónde puede soltar la mano** — y ese es, en una frase, todo el punto de CCDD.\n\n---\n\n**CCDD (Desarrollo Guiado por Contratos de Contexto)** es una alternativa a metodologías tradicionales como SDD (Specification-Driven Development) o TDD (Test-Driven Development), diseñada específicamente para la era de los sistemas no-deterministas (IA Generativa y Agentes).","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#20","metadata":{"content":"d-hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#21","metadata":{"content":"-hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#22","metadata":{"content":"hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#23","metadata":{"content":"ashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#24","metadata":{"content":"shes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#25","metadata":{"content":"hes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#26","metadata":{"content":"es.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#27","metadata":{"content":"s.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#28","metadata":{"content":".json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#29","metadata":{"content":"json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#3","metadata":{"content":"emas no-deterministas (IA Generativa y Agentes).\n\nEn el desarrollo de software clásico, los límites del sistema se definen mediante tipos estáticos y contratos de API (como OpenAPI o Protobuf). En la ingeniería de IA, la única palanca real de control de calidad sobre el comportamiento del modelo es el **contexto**. CCDD eleva el contexto a un artefacto de ingeniería de primer nivel, declarativo, testeable y versionado.\n\n---\n\n## 🧬 El Contrato de Contexto es Híbrido\n\nLa idea distintiva de CCDD es que el contrato de contexto **combina dos naturalezas** que las metodologías tradicionales mantienen separadas, y el flujo de trabajo sabe enrutar cada una a donde corresponde:","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#30","metadata":{"content":"son` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#31","metadata":{"content":"on` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#32","metadata":{"content":"n` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#33","metadata":{"content":"` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#34","metadata":{"content":"en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#35","metadata":{"content":"en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#36","metadata":{"content":"n el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#37","metadata":{"content":"el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#38","metadata":{"content":"el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#39","metadata":{"content":"l repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#4","metadata":{"content":"abajo sabe enrutar cada una a donde corresponde:\n\n| Parte **dura** (determinista, se *verifica*) | Parte **blanda** (probabilística, se *juzga*) |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Estructura, presupuestos de tokens, firmas, reglas | El comportamiento real del modelo |\n| Contexto **estático**: políticas e instrucciones fijas | Contexto **dinámico**: memoria, RAG, entrada del usuario |\n| La valida un **control automático** (gate determinista) | La decide un **humano apoyado por un modelo** |","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#40","metadata":{"content":"repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#41","metadata":{"content":"repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#42","metadata":{"content":"epositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#43","metadata":{"content":"positorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#44","metadata":{"content":"ositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#45","metadata":{"content":"sitorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#46","metadata":{"content":"itorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#47","metadata":{"content":"torio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#48","metadata":{"content":"orio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#49","metadata":{"content":"rio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#5","metadata":{"content":"La decide un **humano apoyado por un modelo** |\n\nEl desarrollo clásico es 100% duro (tipos, compilador) y no sirve para gobernar a un LLM. El \"prompt engineering\" suelto es 100% blando y no es confiable. CCDD es **híbrido**: un contrato que sostiene ambas a la vez, con una regla de oro — *lo verificable se automatiza; lo opinable lo decide una persona, y el modelo informa pero nunca decide.*\n\n---\n\n## 🔄 El Ciclo de Vida CCDD\n\nEl flujo de trabajo CCDD se compone de 5 etapas cíclicas que se ejecutan tanto en tiempo de desarrollo como en integración continua (CI) y tiempo de ejecución (runtime).","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#50","metadata":{"content":"io Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#51","metadata":{"content":"o Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#52","metadata":{"content":"Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#53","metadata":{"content":"Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#54","metadata":{"content":"it.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#55","metadata":{"content":"t.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#56","metadata":{"content":".","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#57","metadata":{"content":"### 3. Integración Continua de Contexto (CCI)\nCada Pull Request que altere las instrucciones del agente o el contrato de contexto activa un paso de verificación **determinista** (sin LLM) en CI:\n- **`diff` de contrato**: compara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#58","metadata":{"content":"**: compara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#59","metadata":{"content":"*: compara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#6","metadata":{"content":"continua (CI) y tiempo de ejecución (runtime).\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[1. Diseñar el Contrato context.yaml] --> B[2. Firmar y Verificar en Local lint]\n    B --> C[3. Integración Continua de Contexto diff & regressions]\n    C --> D[4. Orquestación y Guardrails en Caliente assemble]\n    D --> E[5. Auditoría y Reproducción Bit-a-Bit replay]\n    E --> A\n```","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#60","metadata":{"content":": compara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#61","metadata":{"content":"compara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#62","metadata":{"content":"compara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#63","metadata":{"content":"ompara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#64","metadata":{"content":"mpara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#65","metadata":{"content":"para el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#66","metadata":{"content":"ara el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#67","metadata":{"content":"ra el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#68","metadata":{"content":"a el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#69","metadata":{"content":"el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#7","metadata":{"content":"Reproducción Bit-a-Bit replay]\n    E --> A\n```\n\n### 1. Diseñar el Contrato (`context.yaml`)\nEl desarrollo comienza definiendo los límites de información del agente. En lugar de escribir prompts monolíticos en código:\n- Se definen los **slots** (canales) que alimentarán al modelo.\n- Se establece una jerarquía estricta de **prioridad de atención** (token allocation budget).\n- Se establecen reglas de **compactación** y **guardrails deterministas** (evitar secretos, comprobar referencias, validar formatos JSON).","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#70","metadata":{"content":"el contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#71","metadata":{"content":"l contrato de la rama contra `main`.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#72","metadata":{"content":"contrato de la rama contra `main`. La implementación de referencia aplica **9 reglas deterministas (R1–R9)** que bloquean automáticamente el merge si un cambio debilita la postura del contexto — entre ellas: baja del presupuesto (R1); degradación de prioridad de un slot crítico (R2), que expondría a secuestro de contexto / prompt injection; modificación de un estático firmado sin re-firmar el hash (R4); eliminación o debilitamiento de un guardrail (R9); o cambio de una política sin atestación firmada que alcance el quórum (R6–R8).\n- **El juicio \"blando\" NO vive en el gate.** Decidir si una *reescritura* debilita una política es no-determinista, así que lo hace un **humano** —opcionalmente asistido por un modelo (`review_assist.py`)— *fuera* del camino determinista.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#73","metadata":{"content":"w_assist.py`)— *fuera* del camino determinista. El gate solo verifica firmas; el humano revisa, decide y firma. (Ver especificación `ccdd_spec_v0.3.md` §5.5.)","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#74","metadata":{"content":"(Ver especificación `ccdd_spec_v0.3.md` §5.5.)\n\n### 4. Orquestación y Guardrails en Caliente (Runtime)\nCuando el usuario interactúa con la aplicación en producción:\n- El orquestador CCDD reúne datos dinámicos (memoria, RAG, variables de sesión).\n- El motor de mezcla **asigna dinámicamente los tokens** basándose en la prioridad del contrato. Si el contexto excede el límite del modelo, los slots menos prioritarios son resumidos o truncados automáticamente.\n- El validador ejecuta los guardrails deterministas en milisegundos.\n- **Si pasa la validación:** Se ensambla el payload y se envía al LLM.\n- **Si falla la validación:** Se aborta la ejecución o se enruta a un flujo de contingencia determinista, ahorrando costes de inferencia y previniendo fugas de seguridad.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#75","metadata":{"content":"de inferencia y previniendo fugas de seguridad.\n\n### 5. Auditoría y Reproducción Bit-a-Bit\nEn caso de que el modelo cometa una alucinación o un fallo en producción, CCDD permite la trazabilidad absoluta:\n- El payload ensamblado se firma y registra junto con el verdict de la validación.\n- Los desarrolladores pueden extraer ese snapshot de contexto exacto y reproducir la llamada al LLM **byte-por-byte**, eliminando las variables de drift de base de datos o cambios en el historial.\n\n---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#76","metadata":{"content":"rial.\n\n---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#77","metadata":{"content":"ial.\n\n---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#78","metadata":{"content":"al.\n\n---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#79","metadata":{"content":"l.\n\n---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#8","metadata":{"content":", comprobar referencias, validar formatos JSON).\n\n### 2. Desarrollo Local y Firmas Estáticas\nEl desarrollador escribe los prompts estáticos e instrucciones. El framework CCDD:\n- Genera firmas criptográficas (`SHA-256`) de los archivos estáticos (`system.txt`, `policies.txt`).\n- Ejecuta `lint` en local para garantizar que los prompts no tengan referencias rotas a otros slots y que se ajusten a los presupuestos.\n- Guarda el archivo `expected-hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#80","metadata":{"content":".\n\n---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#81","metadata":{"content":"---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#82","metadata":{"content":"---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#83","metadata":{"content":"---\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#84","metadata":{"content":"--\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#85","metadata":{"content":"-\n\n## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#86","metadata":{"content":"## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#87","metadata":{"content":"## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#88","metadata":{"content":"## 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#89","metadata":{"content":"# 🆚 Comparativa de Metodologías","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"ccdd_workflow.md#9","metadata":{"content":"vo `expected-hashes.json` en el repositorio Git.","okf_concept":"ccdd_workflow.md","okf_type":"Documentation","title":"Context Contract-Driven Development (CCDD)"}},{"id":"